[2026-02-27] ENV_ENGINEER → EXTENSION_BUILDER: Memory leak audit — content-chatgpt.js
  Files: apps/extension/src/content/content-chatgpt.js
  Line 193: titleSpan.addEventListener('mouseenter', ...) — no AbortSignal, no removeEventListener. Leak risk on dynamic span elements.
  Lines 293-298: parentLink.addEventListener('mouseenter/mouseleave', ...) and container.addEventListener('mouseenter/mouseleave', ...) — no AbortSignal. Leak risk when conversation list items are replaced by MutationObserver on navigation.
  Lines 153, 220, 433: SAFE — use { once: true }, AbortController signal, or are one-time DOMContentLoaded setup.
  Recommended fix: Pass AbortSignal from existing _abortController to the mouseenter/mouseleave listeners, OR store refs in hoverButtons Map and removeEventListener on cleanup.
  Priority: ⚠ Medium — does not block functionality, but causes memory growth on long sessions.
  Ref: QA_EXAMINER_audit_final_2026-02-26.md §7.4

